    "note": "WS-5.2 (2026-08-30): CKM_SP800_108_DOUBLE_PIPELINE_KDF did not exist in this engine at all (OpenSSL KBKDF only implements COUNTER and FEEDBACK modes \u2014 see providers/implementations/kdfs/kbkdf.c kbkdf_mode enum \u2014 double pipeline has no meta-provider path). Implemented as a hand-built EVP_MAC round loop (same PRF primitive OpenSSL uses internally): A(0)=fixedInput, A(i)=PRF(Ki,A(i-1)), round output = PRF(Ki, A(i) || counter || fixedInput). Construction verified byte-for-byte against these real ACVP vectors before writing the C++, same as the sibling COUNTER_KDF/FEEDBACK_KDF fixes' methodology. Restricted to \"before fixed data\" counterLocation for the same reason as those two (see sp800_108_kbkdf_test.json). CMAC-TDES excluded (no 3DES-CMAC in this engine)."
  },
